/-- `try_bool_conversion(x::Real)`, `base/multidimensional.jl:1455-1456`.
The inherited numeric interface supplies the Boolean observations of `x == 0`
and `x == 1`, including their errors and state effects. A non-Boolean comparison result in this
conditional context is reported by that observation as `Error.typeError`.
The first true observation returns `true`; only a false first observation
allows the second comparison to run. Only two successful false observations
produce `InexactError(:try_bool_conversion, Bool, x)`, represented by the
existing exception class and function-name fields. This corrects the frozen
helper's Unit-valued success without changing it or supplying a correctness
law for user-defined equality. `m` retains any equality effects before the
second observation or a failure; it may be instantiated with a state monad
whose result retains state on exceptions. Custom overloads of
try_bool_conversion itself are outside this Real fallback method's dispatch,
as stated at lines1452-1454.
-/
def tryBoolConversionChecked {m : Type → Type} [Monad m] [MonadExceptOf Error m]
    {R : Type} (eqZero eqOne : R → m Bool) (x : R) : m Bool := do
  if ← eqZero x then return true
  if ← eqOne x then return true
  throw (.inexactError "try_bool_conversion")

